# SRG-APP-000224-WSR-000136  -  CAT II
# The web server must generate unique session identifiers that cannot be
# reliably reproduced.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000224-WSR-000136
group:           V-206400
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-001188
control_rev5:    SC-23

contribution:    Splunk Enterprise generates session identifiers in its own session
                 subsystem, and placing the instance in FIPS mode constrains the random
                 number generator that subsystem draws on. Whether the generator can be
                 made to repeat an identifier is a property of the product's
                 implementation, not a setting.

governs:         splunk-launch.conf - Environment settings read before Splunk starts, including whether it
                 starts in FIPS mode.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS in 1|true|t|yes (matched case-insensitively)
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
corrected:       splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS equals 1 -> splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS in 1|true|t|yes (matched case-insensitively)
vendor:          splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/splunk-launch.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] tools.sessions.on https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
retired_check:   web.conf [settings] tools.sessions.on equals true
                 reason: The spec states the setting as a literal rather than a type:
                         "tools.sessions.on = true. Whether or not user session support is
                         enabled. Always set this to true." No default is stated.
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Non-reproducibility of the generator, which the check verifies by
                 generating two identifiers from the same input - a product implementation
                 property, verified by vendor attestation or by observation, with no
                 configuration surface
external:        The kernel entropy source feeding the random number generator - operating
                 system

citation:        splunk-launch.conf.spec:110-116 (SPLUNK_FIPS = [0|1], FIPS 140-2
                 algorithms and restrictions); web.conf.spec:920-922 (tools.sessions.on =
                 true, "Always set this to true")
finding:         FIPS mode is not enabled or session support is not enabled, so the
                 application does not constrain session identifier generation to a FIPS
                 140-2 random source to the extent the product allows.
